0457: SweetFramebuffer: a present that costs milliseconds at 2x, a pointer that never leaves the panel, steady
60 Hz ticks; SweetHID: a summon swipe a finger can make.

S5u 2026-11-15 (2x: 1440x2960 canvas, hands-on): "super slow", a flickering pointer, the swipe up never showed
the keyboard. S5a's log: every frame cost 63 ms in the vsync thread although almost no row had changed
("avg_copy_us=62956", rows redrawn 1427 of 228000): the changed-row test (0449) used the kernel's memcmp, a byte
loop, over 17 MB. Frames came 97-133 ms apart (7.5 a second), each tick was armed after the work of the last,
and for those 63 ms the pointer was off the panel (restored before the frame, blended in after it).

- sweet_fb_row_same(): 64 bytes a step in 64-bit words instead of memcmp.
- A full frame on the 1:1 canvas is compared and copied in four bands, on the caller and the three copy helper
  threads (sweet_fb_run_bands, sweet_fb_diff_band).
- The pointer is composed (pointerCompose): its rectangle is written once with final pixels, from the saved
  frame (sweet_fb_prev) and the pointer surface; a frame does not write into that rectangle (the hole in
  scaledCopy / sweet_fb_diff_band). The save-under path stays for the time before the first full frame and for
  partial layer-0 updates.
- armVsync(): ticks at fixed 1/60 s deadlines. Use with sweetfb_hz=60 (a present every tick).
- 0450's "SWEET FB DIRTY" diagnostic is gone (answered: the swap record carries no damage).
- Summon swipe: begins in the bottom 170 px (was 70 = 3 mm), 170 px up within 700 ms, more up than sideways;
  anything else in that zone is handed to the trackpad from its first point (taps there still click). Logs
  "SWEET KBD: show (swipe up from ...)" / "not the swipe (...)".

Host test: scratch fbtest (the present path cut from this file, random frames / pointer moves / hides /
keyboard shows against an independent rendering, 1:1 and scaled, ASan+UBSan).
Kernel seq2c = seq2b + 0457.

